## 3. System‑Level Power Budget and Flight Time

**Take‑off mass:** 1.35 kg (frame 300 g, battery 350 g, motors 4×65 g, electronics 200 g, payload 200 g).  
**Hover thrust:** ~13.5 N, requiring ~250 W electrical power (motors+ESCs).  
**Avionics:** Jetson 5 W, STM32 + sensors 2 W. Total 257 W.

**Battery:** 6S 2200 mAh LiPo (22.2 V × 2.2 Ah = 48.8 Wh). Usable energy (80% DoD): 39 Wh.  
**Hover flight time:** 39 Wh / 257 W ≈ 9.1 minutes.  
**Cruise (100 W):** 39 Wh / 100 W ≈ 23 minutes.

Jetson operation at 5 W is maintained for the full mission. Thermal throttling reduces compute before increasing flight time.

