## 4. Software Architecture

### 4.1 High‑Level Software (Jetson Orin Nano)

```
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│   PC‑SRGI Inference Engine (Rust)              │
│   · TensorRT‑optimized ONNX model              │
│   · CAN‑FD driver (SocketCAN)                  │
│   · Thermal / power monitor                    │
│   · Data logger (microSD)                      │
└───────────────┬────────────────────────────────┘
                │ (shared memory)
┌───────────────▼────────────────────────────────┐
│   Training & Analysis (Python)                 │
│   · PyTorch model definition / training        │
│   · Differentiable Lie‑group integrator        │
│   · Symbolic extraction (PySR)                 │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

**Inference budget:** Control loop runs at 500 Hz → 2 ms period. Neural inference must complete within **1.5 ms**, leaving 0.5 ms for transmission and overhead.  
**Model design constraint:** The transformer + capsule network is sized to meet this budget. **Before first flight, the exported ONNX model must be profiled on the Jetson Orin Nano with TensorRT. If latency exceeds 1.5 ms, mitigation steps include reducing transformer layers to 1, halving d_model to 32, or switching to an LSTM. The fallback loop frequency is 250 Hz (4 ms budget).**  
Preliminary profiling of comparable small‑footprint models (e.g., DistilBERT‑tiny) on Orin Nano suggests that a 2‑layer transformer with d_model=64 and H=5 can be executed in under 1.5 ms with FP16 and TensorRT, but confirmation is mandatory.

### 4.2 Low‑Level Software (STM32H7)

```
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│   FreeRTOS Kernel                              │
├────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│   Tasks (priority):                            │
│   · Sensor Fusion EKF (500 Hz)                 │
│   · CAN‑FD RX/TX (1 kHz interrupt)             │
│   · Watchdog Monitor (1 kHz)                   │
│   · Control Mixer (PWM generation)             │
│   · Safety Monitor (command validation)        │
│   · MAVLink telemetry (optional)               │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

**Safety layers:**

| Layer | Mechanism | Response Time |
|---|---|---|
| 1. Physical Clamping | PWM saturation in mixer | < 10 µs |
| 2. Command Validation | Rate & magnitude checks | < 100 µs |
| 3. Software Watchdog | Multi‑task heartbeat monitor | < 1 ms |
| 4. Hardware Watchdog | Independent IWDG (32 kHz clock) | < 10 ms |
| 5. Manual RC Override | Direct SBUS → PWM passthrough | < 5 ms |

**Watchdog details:** Each FreeRTOS task increments a dedicated atomic counter. A separate watchdog task checks all counters every 1 ms. If any counter fails to advance within 5 ms, the system switches to PID fallback and disables neural commands. The hardware IWDG is refreshed only if all tasks are healthy; otherwise it resets the entire flight controller.

