## 10. Sim‑to‑Real Transfer Strategy

**Procedure:**

1. **System‑identification flight:** Fly with PID controller for ≥5 minutes, logging state, control, and EKF velocity.
2. **Compute true residual:** \( F_{\text{res,true}} = m \dot{v}_{\text{est}} - f_{\text{cons}}(s) - f_{\text{ctrl}}(u) \). The velocity derivative is obtained from the EKF via filtered finite differences.
3. **Fine‑tune capsule layer offline:** Freeze transformer and primitive parameters; update only gate logits and basis vectors on real flight data.
4. **Stopping criterion:** Training stops when the force residual RMSE < 0.5 N and torque RMSE < 0.05 N·m on a held‑out validation segment. (The residual estimation noise floor is ≈0.14 N (1σ), so 0.5 N corresponds to >3σ, reliably detectable.)
5. **Activation:** Once the criterion is met, activate the full PC‑SRGI controller with gain 1.0. A single verification flight confirms stability.

---

## 11. Safety and Verification

- **Command validation:** Thrust ∈ [0, max_thrust], torques bounded, rate‑limited. Three consecutive violations trigger fallback.
- **Energy drift monitor:** STM32 computes \( E_{\text{cons}} \) at 100 Hz; if drift exceeds 0.1 J in 1 s without control power, fallback.
- **Watchdog:** Software watchdog monitors all tasks; hardware IWDG resets board if software hangs.
- **Manual override:** SBUS RC receiver provides direct motor passthrough via a dedicated switch.

