## 13. Regulatory Pathway (Realistic Near‑Term)

All initial flights will be conducted **within visual line‑of‑sight (VLOS)** under **FAA Part 107** (or equivalent national regulations). The drone is registered, the pilot holds a Remote Pilot Certificate, and the operation is conducted in uncontrolled airspace or at a designated UAS test site. A Remote ID broadcast module (e.g., Dronetag Mini) is installed. For any future autonomous beyond‑visual‑line‑of‑sight (BVLOS) missions, a separate Certificate of Waiver or Authorization (COA) will be obtained through institutional channels, following ASTM F3312 risk assessment—this is not required for v4.1. Geo‑fencing and auto‑land on egress are implemented in the STM32 fallback layer.

