## Appendix K: Physical Feature Vector (Final, Corrected)

The feature vector \( \xi \in \mathbb{R}^{20} \) is computed deterministically from the current state \( s \) and control \( u \). All quantities are in SI units; scaling factors bring the typical range to ≈ [‑1, 1] for stable training.

| Idx | Feature | Formula / Source | Scaling | Typical Scaled Range | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Body velocity x | \( v_{b,x} = (R^\top v)_x \) | 1/10 | ±1.5 (max 15 m/s) | Drag components |
| 2 | Body velocity y | \( v_{b,y} \) | 1/10 | ±1.5 | |
| 3 | Body velocity z | \( v_{b,z} \) | 1/5 | ±2 (max 10 m/s vert.) | Also used for vertical drag |
| 4 | Speed (norm) | \( \|v_b\| \) | 1/15 | 0–1 (max 15 m/s) | |
| 5 | Angle of attack proxy | \( \frac{v_{b,z}}{\sqrt{v_{b,x}^2+v_{b,y}^2} + \epsilon} \) | — | ±1 ( \( \epsilon = 0.1 \) m/s) | |
| 6 | Body angular rate x | \( \omega_x \) | 1/5 | ±1 (max 5 rad/s) | |
| 7 | Body angular rate y | \( \omega_y \) | 1/5 | ±1 | |
| 8 | Body angular rate z | \( \omega_z \) | 1/5 | ±1 | |
| 9 | Angular rate norm | \( \|\omega\| \) | 1/8 | 0–1 (max 8 rad/s) | |
|10 | Altitude above ground | \( z_{\text{AGL}} \) (from baro/flow) | 1/5 | 0–2 (0–10 m) | Ground effect |
|11 | Vertical speed | \( \dot{z}_{\text{AGL}} \) (EKF) | 1/3 | ±2 (max 6 m/s) | |
|12 | Dynamic pressure | \( \frac{1}{2}\rho \|v_b\|^2 \) | 1/100 | 0–1.38 (ρ=1.225) | Max ~138 Pa |
|13 | Thrust command | \( T_{\text{cmd}} \) (normalised 0‑1) | 10 | 0–10 | Allows nonlinear motor curve |
|14 | Torque cmd x | \( \tau_x \) (N·m) | 100 | ±2 (max 0.02 N·m) | Scaled to bring ±0.02→±2 |
|15 | Torque cmd y | \( \tau_y \) (N·m) | 100 | ±2 | |
|16 | Torque cmd z | \( \tau_z \) (N·m) | 100 | ±2 | |
|17 | Torque norm | \( \|\tau\| \) (N·m) | 100 | 0–~3.5 | |
|18 | Body accel residual | \( a_{\text{res}} = \dot{v}_b - g \) (EKF, filtered 20 Hz) | 1/10 | ±1 (max 10 m/s²) | Direct indicator of external force |
|19 | Advance ratio proxy | \( \lambda = \frac{\|v_{b,xy}\|}{k_\omega \sqrt{T_{\text{cmd}}+\epsilon}} \) | 1/0.5 | 0–2 | \( k_\omega = 0.089\cdot 400 \), see below |
|20 | Constant | 1.0 | — | 1.0 | Bias |

**Feature 19 – detailed derivation:**  
Rotor angular velocity estimated from static thrust: \( T_{\text{max}} T_{\text{cmd}} = 4 k_T \omega_{\text{prop}}^2 \). With \( T_{\text{max}} = 15 \) N, \( k_T = 1.2\times10^{-5} \) N/RPM²,  
\[
\omega_{\text{prop}} \approx \sqrt{\frac{15\,T_{\text{cmd}}}{4\cdot1.2\times10^{-5}}} = 400\sqrt{T_{\text{cmd}}}\ \text{rad/s}.
\]  
Propeller radius \( r = 0.089 \) m, so blade tip speed \( v_{\text{tip}} = r\omega_{\text{prop}} \). The advance ratio proxy is  
\[
\lambda = \frac{\|v_{b,xy}\|}{v_{\text{tip}}} = \frac{\|v_{b,xy}\|}{0.089\cdot 400\sqrt{T_{\text{cmd}}}} = \frac{\|v_{b,xy}\|}{35.6\sqrt{T_{\text{cmd}}}}.
\]  
For numerical stability, use \( \epsilon = 0.01 \). Scaling 1/0.5 brings typical λ (up to ~1) to a range 0–2.

**Feature 18 – note:** The body acceleration residual is computed from the EKF velocity estimate (low‑pass filtered at 20 Hz) minus the gravity vector in body frame. It provides the network with a direct measurement of the total external force, speeding up learning.

All features are computed at each inference step. The scaling factors have been chosen such that the inputs to the capsule primitives are roughly in the range [-1, 1], aiding training stability.

